Foodiy Source-Available License (FSAL) v1.1
============================================

Copyright (c) 2026 Filippo Mattia Menghi <filippo@menghi.dev>
GitHub: https://github.com/Cyberfilo/foodiy

This is NOT an OSI-approved open-source license. It is a source-available
license with user-count caps, notification obligations, and commercial-use
restrictions. Please read in full before using this software.

Changes from v1.0 to v1.1:
  - New three-tier model: Personal, Community Development, Commercial.
  - Explicit per-deployment user caps (fewer than 10 for Personal, fewer
    than 25 for Community Development).
  - Commercial use now requires BOTH notification AND inclusion of The
    Author as a participating party in the commercial arrangement.
  - Author contact updated to filippo@menghi.dev.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DEFINITIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"The Software" means the source code, documentation, configuration, and
assets contained in this repository, and any portion thereof.

"The Author" means Filippo Mattia Menghi, the copyright holder, reachable at
filippo@menghi.dev or via GitHub issues at
https://github.com/Cyberfilo/foodiy/issues.

"You" (or "Your") means the individual or entity exercising rights under
this license.

"Derivative Work" means any work that incorporates, copies, modifies,
adapts, translates, or builds upon The Software, in whole or in part,
including but not limited to forks, modified redistributions, hosted
instances, and reimplementations that copy substantial logic, structure,
or assets from The Software.

"Active Deployment" means any running instance of The Software or a
Derivative Work hosted on any infrastructure (local, private cloud, public
cloud, on-device, or otherwise) that is reachable by one or more human
users with the intent of being used. Deployments used solely as throwaway
sandboxes for a single developer's testing, created and destroyed within a
short period and never shared with other humans, are not counted as Active
Deployments for the purposes of the user caps in Section 2.

"User" of an Active Deployment means any distinct human who has an
account, profile, credential, or otherwise-identifiable presence on that
deployment, including the operator of the deployment. Automated bots,
system processes, and headless test accounts do not count.

"Commercial Use" means any use of The Software or a Derivative Work that:
  (a) is bundled with, incorporated into, or provided as a product or
      service offered for sale, rent, subscription, or any other form of
      monetary consideration;
  (b) is hosted, deployed, or otherwise made available to users in a
      manner exceeding the caps set out in Section 2;
  (c) is intended, in whole or in part, to generate revenue, advertising
      income, sponsorship, or any other monetary or non-monetary benefit
      beyond personal or community-development use;
  (d) is performed by, for, or on behalf of a for-profit entity acting in
      a business capacity, or by an individual acting in a commercial
      capacity; or
  (e) is used internally by a for-profit entity for business operations
      that are themselves revenue-generating or customer-facing.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THREE-TIER GRANT OF RIGHTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Subject to the conditions of Sections 3–6, The Author grants You a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license
to use The Software under EXACTLY ONE of the following tiers at a time.
Moving between tiers requires satisfying the conditions of the destination
tier.

============================================
2.A  PERSONAL TIER — "friends and family"
============================================

You may, without fee:
  (a) view, fork, clone, and download The Software;
  (b) modify The Software for Your personal use;
  (c) run ONE OR MORE Active Deployments of The Software or a Derivative
      Work, PROVIDED THAT each such Active Deployment has FEWER THAN TEN
      (< 10) Users at any point in its lifetime.

"Friends and family" scope: the Personal Tier is intended to cover running
a deployment for Yourself and a small circle of people you know personally
(family, friends, housemates, a small private group). It does not cover
paying customers, external clients, the general public, or anyone whose
access is offered in exchange for any form of consideration.

Conditions specific to the Personal Tier:
  (i)  You MUST notify The Author per Section 3 on Your first deployment.
  (ii) If any one Active Deployment would cross the 10-User threshold, You
       must either reduce it below the cap, migrate to the Community
       Development Tier (if eligible), or obtain Commercial-Use approval
       per Section 2.C before the threshold is crossed.

============================================
2.B  COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT TIER — "collaborate, improve, share"
============================================

You may, without fee:
  (a) fork The Software and publish Your fork for non-commercial
      development purposes;
  (b) invite other contributors to collaborate on Your fork;
  (c) run ONE OR MORE Active Deployments of Your Derivative Work
      (e.g. a staging / beta / community instance), PROVIDED THAT each
      such Active Deployment has FEWER THAN TWENTY-FIVE (< 25) Users at
      any point in its lifetime;
  (d) distribute the modified source code of Your Derivative Work under
      this same FSAL v1.1 license (no relicensing — see Section 5).

Conditions specific to the Community Development Tier:
  (i)  You MUST notify The Author per Section 3 on Your first fork AND
       each time You publish a materially changed version (whether to a
       public repository, a deployment, or a distribution channel). A
       "material change" means any change that alters behavior observable
       to end users, introduces a new integration, or affects nutritional
       calculations, scoring, or data handling. Routine dependency bumps
       and non-functional refactors are exempt.
  (ii) You MAY NOT make Commercial Use of Your Derivative Work while
       operating under this tier. Moving to Commercial Use requires the
       process in Section 2.C.
  (iii) You MUST keep this LICENSE file in Your fork and comply with the
        attribution clause in Section 5.

Upstream contributions (pull requests back to
https://github.com/Cyberfilo/foodiy) are encouraged but not required.

============================================
2.C  COMMERCIAL TIER — "revenue / scale / business use"
============================================

Commercial Use is PROHIBITED unless The Author has:
  (i)  been NOTIFIED in advance in writing; AND
  (ii) been INCLUDED as a participating party in the commercial
       arrangement.

"Included" means The Author is a formally recognised party to the
arrangement, with terms to be negotiated in good faith between You and
The Author. These terms MAY include, without limitation: attribution,
credit, co-authorship of Derivative Works, a revenue share, an equity
stake, a board/advisor seat, licensing fees, or any combination thereof.
The specific form of inclusion is subject to The Author's consent and
may be tailored to the nature and scale of the commercial activity.

To initiate the Commercial Tier, send a written request to
filippo@menghi.dev with the subject line beginning
"[FOODIY-FSAL COMMERCIAL REQUEST]" and containing:
  (a) a clear description of the intended Commercial Use;
  (b) the entity that will conduct the Commercial Use;
  (c) the expected scale (projected users, revenue, geography);
  (d) a proposal for how The Author will be included (attribution, revenue
      share, equity, advisory, or other), or a note that You wish The
      Author to propose terms.

The Author may grant, decline, negotiate, or condition such permission
at The Author's sole discretion. Silence by The Author is NOT consent:
absence of a written response within sixty (60) days of Your request is
treated as a denial.

Commercial Tier permission, once granted, applies only to the specific
Commercial Use described in the request, and is not transferable to other
uses, entities, or successors without a new approval.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. MANDATORY NOTIFICATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Regardless of tier, any ONE of the events below triggers an obligation to
notify The Author in writing within thirty (30) days:

  (a) Your first fork, clone-with-intent-to-modify, or Derivative Work;
  (b) Your first Active Deployment;
  (c) Any material change to a published Derivative Work
      (Community Development Tier only);
  (d) Any change in the nature or scale of Your use (e.g., moving from
      Personal Tier to Community Development Tier);
  (e) Any intended transition to Commercial Use (use the Section 2.C
      process instead of plain notification).

Each notification must include:
  (i)   Your legal name or GitHub username (or both);
  (ii)  a URL pointing to Your fork or Derivative Work, if any;
  (iii) the tier under which You are operating;
  (iv)  a brief, good-faith description of how You are using or intend to
        use The Software;
  (v)   Your contact email address.

Notification is satisfied by any ONE of the following:
  - Email to filippo@menghi.dev with the subject line beginning
    "[FOODIY-FSAL]".
  - Opening a GitHub issue at
    https://github.com/Cyberfilo/foodiy/issues with the title beginning
    "[FSAL Notification]" and containing the information above.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. USER-CAP ENFORCEMENT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You are solely responsible for monitoring the User count of each Active
Deployment You operate. The Author may, on reasonable request, require
You to produce evidence that Your deployment(s) are within the applicable
cap (for example, a current user count exported from Your deployment's
admin tools). If a deployment exceeds its tier's cap:

  (a) You must reduce the user count below the cap within fourteen (14)
      days, OR
  (b) You must initiate the Commercial Tier process per Section 2.C,
      OR
  (c) Your license terminates for that deployment per Section 7.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. ATTRIBUTION AND LICENSE PROPAGATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Any Derivative Work must:

  (a) retain this LICENSE file, unmodified, in its source tree;
